<%# /privacy: the Privacy Policy, written from what this app does. Every
    statement of practice rests on a file named in the README's "Legal pages"
    table; change the practice and this page changes with it. Rantly has no
    accounts, no database, no forms and no cookies today, so this page says so;
    the day it gains any of them, this page is wrong until it is edited. -%>
<% content_for(:title, "Privacy Policy") %>
<% content_for(:description, "What Rantly collects, which is very little, and who else sees it.") %>

<article class="card legal" data-legal-page="privacy" aria-labelledby="legal-title">
  <header class="legal__head">
    <h1 id="legal-title" class="legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: October 3, 2026</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p>McRitchie Studio LLC, doing business as McRitchie Studio ("McRitchie Studio", "we", "us"), operates Rantly at <a href="https://rantly.mcritchie.studio">rantly.mcritchie.studio</a> (the "Site").</p>
    <p>Rantly is a showcase: a working demonstration of a social network with a 140-character minimum. Every user, rant and comment on it is fictional sample data that we wrote. This policy explains what the Site collects from you, which is very little, and who else receives it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. What We Collect</h2>
    <p><strong>No accounts.</strong> The Site has no sign-up, no sign-in and no passwords. We do not ask for your name, your email address or anything else about you.</p>
    <p><strong>Nothing you type.</strong> The rant box on the home page is a demonstration. It counts your characters in your browser and sends nothing: there is no form behind it, and what you type is not posted, saved or seen by us. Commenting is switched off.</p>
    <p><strong>Server logs.</strong> Like any website, the servers that deliver the Site record each request: your IP address, the page you asked for, the time, and technical details of the request such as your browser's description of itself. We use these logs only to keep the Site running and to find faults.</p>
    <p><strong>If you email us.</strong> If you write to the address below, we receive your email address and whatever your message contains, and we use them only to reply.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
    <p>The Site sets no cookies. It runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts, and it does not use your browser's storage.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Who Else Receives It</h2>
    <p>We do not sell, rent or share your information. The Site is hosted by <strong>Heroku</strong> (Salesforce), which delivers its pages and keeps the server logs described above on our behalf.</p>
    <p>The Site's pages load nothing from other companies: no fonts, maps, videos or scripts. A few links lead to other sites, such as GitHub and mcritchie.studio. Those sites receive your visit only if you follow the link, under their own privacy policies.</p>
    <p>We may disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect the rights, safety and property of McRitchie Studio or others.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Security</h2>
    <p>The Site is served only over an encrypted connection (HTTPS): a visit on plain HTTP is redirected to it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Children</h2>
    <p>The Site is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Your Choices</h2>
    <p>You can use the whole Site without giving us anything. If you have emailed us and want that correspondence deleted, or have a question about this policy, write to <a href="mailto:team@mcritchie.studio">team@mcritchie.studio</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>If Rantly ever gains accounts or saves what you write, this policy will change before it does. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when it was last revised.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>McRitchie Studio LLC<br>Email: <a href="mailto:team@mcritchie.studio">team@mcritchie.studio</a></p>
  </section>
</article>
